# Topic 3 · Feminist Movements — the West, the United Nations and Pakistan

> Syllabus head IV. 126 one-liners, 22 past MCQs and 32 practice MCQs.

The past MCQs centre on three things: the UN conferences (Mexico 1975, Beijing 1995), CEDAW and Pakistan's accession in 1996, and APWA and the Hudood Ordinances. The practice set adds the suffrage story, the second and fourth waves, the UN machinery, the Pakistan Movement's women and the movement of the 1980s.

